{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545730-2e-how-rapt-enraptured-mad-are-powerful-nameless-and-accursed","id":1545730,"title":"[2E] How Rapt/Enraptured/Mad are powerful? [Nameless and Accursed]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-12T00:12:18-08:00","id":1545730,"title":"[2E] How Rapt/Enraptured/Mad are powerful? [Nameless and Accursed]","content":"<b>I wonder how powerful are Rapt/Enraptured </b>( previouslu known Mad ) compared to other mages? How Rapt are they have been avoiding detection all these years? They are literally killing people left and right with magic, don't they? And somehow they live all the years in secret in Pentacle structures... \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T05:21:45-08:00","id":1545740,"title":"","content":"Nameless and Accursed answers these questions. They add free Occultation dots equal to their current Stress, lose their sympathetic name, have their existence subject to Quiescence, gain a Magical Savant ability relating to their Fault, and the most common type of Enraptured mage is both easy to think of as just a more extreme version of a regular mage and as capable of having former friends/peers/mentors/students/loved ones cover for them for individual reasons both selfish and compassionate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T08:21:52-08:00","id":1545741,"title":"","content":"I wonder <b>how Consillia reacts to</b> 'typical' <b><i>Malefactors</i></b> - VIOLENT serial killer Rapt? ( NOT the more gentle Savants. ) <b>Consillia kill them after trial</b> - or generally take out their souls with Death magics, to end possibility of return of Enrapture? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-12-2024, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T09:10:35-08:00","id":1545742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed, page 65</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The responsibility of dealing with a friend or ally who succumbs to Rapture is a heavy one. Alerting the Orders or Consilium could well sentence her to death, and it\u2019s hard to sign a<br /> friend\u2019s execution order.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it seems that normally a kill order is immediately issued, even amongst the Pyramid. No Rapt is truly safe, not even the Savants. These are mages that will commit any abuse of Sleepers and Awakened to further their Fault, they will use any resource they can find, wield any methods.<br /> <br /> You cannot easily contain or redirect their focus either. As Stress builds, they become more desperate to get out there and continue their work. They are difficult to find by scrying, tracking down their sympathetic name does nothing and Sleepers forget their passage. Even if they make an effort to contain themselves, a Tulpa will eventually manifest and try to push hard for them to pursue their Fault.<br /> <br /> A kinder Consilium would call the Bellerophon Group, provided they know they exist. However, even when the specialist have prepared for all of the above, they are still dealing with a highly volatile and unfettered mage. Doubly so because they need to keep this up while they try to help them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T09:20:11-08:00","id":1545743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545730-2e-how-rapt-enraptured-mad-are-powerful-nameless-and-accursed?p=1545741#post1545741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder <b>how Consillia reacts to</b> 'typical' VIOLENT serial killer Rapt? ( NOT the more gentle Savants. ) <b>Consillia kill them after trial</b> - or generally take out their souls with Death magics, to end possibility of return of Enrapture? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rapt are rare enough that Left-Hand Path states many Consilia go centuries without Enraptured activity, and the Bellerophon Group is an organization formed less than a hundred years ago specifically to research the Rapt. It would come down to Silver Laws at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-12-2024, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T03:28:58-08:00","id":1545777,"title":"","content":"I think Malefactors have a potential for some more variety than just being spree murderers, even within the confines of an inciting Act of Hubris that was based on murder. After all, the kind of impulsive murder that constitutes Hurbis against Falling Wisdom will often have more sophisticated context than &quot;just because&quot;; imagine a mage who did it because, in the course of investigating some unrelated Mystery, they stumble upon some person who has committed a truly heinous act that they got away with to anybody lacking preternatural senses, and the urge to just destroy them in retribution burst out. The Fault that results from that may be a lot more focused on punishment for certain actions in a way that might limit their excesses and put them in places that many other Awakened won't be looking at (and maybe if they did might still not quite be eager to expose).<br /> <br /> Still, there do seem to be those Rapt who are a lot less inhibited and deadly, and the answer to the question of &quot;how do they not get exposed and eliminated quickly&quot; is probably... they don't, and that's part of why the Awakened know so little about the Rapt even after thousands of years. That probably the most visible ones get seen first in terms of people flagrantly committing crimes in ways that end up with them either being killed as punishment or in the course of trying to take them captive, and in the process eliminating most of the evidence that can be used to understand why they were doing that. As a concept, the Rapt isn't really something that needs to rely on a premise of them easily flying under the radar; that many or most of them have short life expectancies does not reduce the incidence of people falling to Rapture, and may in fact increase it as it facilitates more ignorance of the risks.<br /> <br /> As for the Bellerophan Group, I'm not really seeing that as an organisation that one can call in to deal with something like they were the Ghostbusters. I think it's more like a network of likeminded mages that recognised this particular hole in the threat awareness of Pentacle society and have been dedicated to the slow process of keeping an eye out for where it occurs to attempt some systematic investigation. You don't summon members of the Group when you realise there's a problem caused by a Rapt, somebody shows up if they catch wind of such a thing to try and get some research in. It's possible that a Consilium only even realises that the problem is being caused by a Rapt mage when somebody with Bellerophon Group credentials arrives in pursuit and puts together a good case for it. If a mage actively calls upon another mage whom they know is part of the Group, I would expect that to be a purely personal contact based on some shared past experience with Rapture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T04:27:08-08:00","id":1545780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545730-2e-how-rapt-enraptured-mad-are-powerful-nameless-and-accursed?p=1545777#post1545777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Malefactors have a potential for some more variety than just being spree murderers, even within the confines of an inciting Act of Hubris that was based on murder. After all, the kind of impulsive murder that constitutes Hurbis against Falling Wisdom will often have more sophisticated context than &quot;just because&quot;; imagine a mage who did it because, in the course of investigating some unrelated Mystery, they stumble upon some person who has committed a truly heinous act that they got away with to anybody lacking preternatural senses, and the urge to just destroy them in retribution burst out. The Fault that results from that may be a lot more focused on punishment for certain actions in a way that might limit their excesses and put them in places that many other Awakened won't be looking at (and maybe if they did might still not quite be eager to expose).<br /> <br /> Still, there do seem to be those Rapt who are a lot less inhibited and deadly, and the answer to the question of &quot;how do they not get exposed and eliminated quickly&quot; is probably... they don't, and that's part of why the Awakened know so little about the Rapt even after thousands of years. That probably the most visible ones get seen first in terms of people flagrantly committing crimes in ways that end up with them either being killed as punishment or in the course of trying to take them captive, and in the process eliminating most of the evidence that can be used to understand why they were doing that. As a concept, the Rapt isn't really something that needs to rely on a premise of them easily flying under the radar; that many or most of them have short life expectancies does not reduce the incidence of people falling to Rapture, and may in fact increase it as it facilitates more ignorance of the risks.<br /> <br /> As for the Bellerophan Group, I'm not really seeing that as an organisation that one can call in to deal with something like they were the Ghostbusters. I think it's more like a network of likeminded mages that recognised this particular hole in the threat awareness of Pentacle society and have been dedicated to the slow process of keeping an eye out for where it occurs to attempt some systematic investigation. You don't summon members of the Group when you realise there's a problem caused by a Rapt, somebody shows up if they catch wind of such a thing to try and get some research in. It's possible that a Consilium only even realises that the problem is being caused by a Rapt mage when somebody with Bellerophon Group credentials arrives in pursuit and puts together a good case for it. If a mage actively calls upon another mage whom they know is part of the Group, I would expect that to be a purely personal contact based on some shared past experience with Rapture.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Rapt Punisher, that is a very cool concept. You could even have them as a fallen interfector that the Guardians keep under close supervision, very effective at their job, but just as likely to do horrible things in their indignation against their targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T07:30:45-08:00","id":1545788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545730-2e-how-rapt-enraptured-mad-are-powerful-nameless-and-accursed?p=1545780#post1545780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Rapt Punisher, that is a very cool concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I was going for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could even have them as a fallen interfector that the Guardians keep under close supervision, very effective at their job</div> </div> </div> </div>The job of the Interfector is to carry out sentence on people who have been taken captive, tried, and sentenced. Being effective at it means being quick and efficient, without hesitation or sentiment, but also without enthusiasm. Being Rapt seems like it would in all ways be a liability to that in the eyes of other mages, especially of the Guardians.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that the path of hubris that leads to somebody having a Fault such as this seems quite contrary to somebody having been effective as an Interfector in the first place. Certainly, the act itself and the Rapture that results from it are not indicative of the traits somebody would look for in such a position.<br /> <br /> I could see a scenario where a Rapt Interfector is somebody that a cabal including deeply compromised Guardians might choose to protect after their condition becomes known, but even that I would picture as people convincing themselves that somebody's Rapture is not a detriment to them doing unrelated Interfector duties, rather than actively beneficial to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">just as likely to do horrible things in their indignation against their targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though mages are liable to very closely scrutinise how justice is carried out against their own, and an Interfector who does something cruel and unusual in the process of carrying it out is going to be noticed immediately.<br /> <br /> The Interfector might be anonymous, but the role is so solemn and public, it seems like the last place any Rapt should be able to hide, let alone thrive.<br /> <br /> (Also keeping in mind that, at least per the definition provided in the Second Edition core, there are more sentences carried out by Interfectors than just execution.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}